From: Matus <dichhead@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:36:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] hw/display: add apv-gpu-proxy, a vmapple GPU served by
 another process

aquarat's apv-gpu-proxy (aquarat/qemu-reims-vgpu) maps vmapple's
paravirtual GPU windows and forwards them to a backend process such as
Reims' reims-vgpu-backend, which renders the guest's Metal through the
host's Vulkan.  vmapple's new gfx-device property picks apple-gfx-mmio,
apv-gpu-proxy or none.
